Hi,

here's v1.1 with a couple of minor things Sashiko reported here:

https://sashiko.dev/#/message/20260613185632.GAai2n4GkGXFsBm6gT%40fat_crate.local

which I forgot to clean up as part of the removal.

I've kept the Acked-by:'s because nothing really changes to the intent and the
code is the same - changes are mostly comments removal and X86_FEATURE_UP
which is not needed anymore and is freeing one slot in the synthetic map.

Thx.

---
From: "Borislav Petkov (AMD)" <bp@alien8.de>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 10:15:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] x86/alternative: Drop smp_locks glue

This was there to be able to patch out locking instructions when running
a SMP kernel build on a UP CPU. The times are long gone when single-CPU
x86 machines were relevant so drop that machinery and simplify the code
considerably.

LOCK_PREFIX needs to stay for when one wants to do a UP build for
whatever reason. That'll go away when CONFIG_SMP becomes unconditional.

Kill a bunch of leftover, unused prototypes while at it.

Signed-off-by: Borislav Petkov (AMD) <bp@alien8.de>
Acked-by: Peter Zijlstra (Intel) <peterz@infradead.org>
